{"kind":"request","text":"State refactor S4: separate parked scheduling and reply custody in the outside-effect driver\n\nThis is item 4 from the implicit-state shortlist in a99e32d9, audited at e50d9eeb. packages/scope/src/operations.ts has not changed since the audit, at origin/main c85553da. Ruling 217e53e9 releases the hold. Run it in lane C under 0d6d0fba, from origin/main c85553da.\n\nThe driver's one class holds dispatch together with two other jobs, and each job keeps its own memory-only state:\n- Parked scheduling: #walk (the walk over attempts with no time to look at them next), #waiting (attempts not ready under OperationRules.ready), #refused (kinds the outside port did not accept), and the store.parked page.\n- Reply custody: #held (answers in hand that the scope could not record yet) and #replyMore (a retained-reply page has a successor).\nThe wake decision near line 542 reads both jobs' state, and so does the run loop near line 378.\n\nIn one head:\n1. Give parked scheduling one owner. It holds the walk, the not-ready flag and the refused kinds. It answers what to look at next and when to wake.\n2. Give reply custody one owner. It holds the answers in hand and the retained-reply paging. It answers which reply to offer next. It never sends.\n3. Keep dispatch, the durable sent mark and the ledger writes in the driver. The driver asks both owners and combines their wake requests in one place.\n\nKeep every current guarantee:\n- The sent mark is durable before an outside mutation, and nothing is sent twice.\n- An attempt with no recorded answer stays unknown, never settled. A lost process loses answers in hand, and the attempt stays a task.\n- An answer in hand wins over a retained reply for the same attempt.\n- A restart looks at every parked attempt once, whatever is due.\n- A reaccepted kind is sent at the next turn without a restart.\n- Cancellation during an await, late completion after retirement, and restart after a durable mark behave as they do now.\n- With nothing due, a pass writes nothing.\n\nKeep diagnoses and their names unchanged, or list each change. Use the existing scope operation and outside-effect owners as witnesses. Add a characterization test only for a guarantee that no current test pins, and name it. Change no archive or fold code. Follow ruling 217e53e9: stop on an archive retry, and report the gate line before review. No state-machine framework or library.\n\nRun the changed tests while you work, and npm run gate once before review, one gate at a time on this machine. Builder only; planner deploys. Never run rm -rf or rm -f.","body":{"conditions":"One reviewed head on main in which the outside-effect driver's parked scheduling and its reply custody each have one owner with its own state, separate from dispatch; the durable sent mark, ledger semantics and every listed guarantee keep a named witness; no archive or fold code changes; changed tests plus one gate before review; the archive-retry line from 217e53e9 is reported; checker-approved and landed.","target_head":"c85553da0b4ec20849cb00965ce69b9372e15405","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}